#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087501 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9849b9-397b-5fb9-bb4b-01f3d013c5c2" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Polygon Under the Action of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/id #uuid "52fc2fee-c015-55e0-b411-03c86d5992e0" :question/math-academy-id "e-5447" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T$, given by\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nThe triangle $\\triangle ABC$ is shown below. Find $\\triangle A'B'C'$, the image of $\\triangle ABC$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/866/Source/Images/8d714d1a8dad0fec63191b436f75f1f2.png)" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $T$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $\\triangle ABC$:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nTX &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of $\\triangle A'B'C'$ are $(-3,-4), (0,0), (1,-2)$, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/866/Source/Images/3ac3afc1cb31f4c0e1cf319acf62a417.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087547 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "85936915-4c9c-572c-af99-025fec0f7570" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Line Segment Under the Action of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/id #uuid "8b7758b4-e0ec-5872-90d7-1136c9716574" :question/math-academy-id "e-6682" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T$, given by\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nThe line segment $\\overline{AB}$ is shown below. Find $\\overline{A'B'}$, the image of $\\overline{AB}$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/866/Source/Images/99de657ac0df287926da7644ba8c7907.png)" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $\\overline{AB}$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the endpoints of $\\overline{AB}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nTX &= \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective endpoints of the image are $A'(1,3)$ and $B'(1,-2)$, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/866/Source/Images/105a1915ca20d2babc4684b44cd6620a.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087935 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9849b9-397b-5fb9-bb4b-01f3d013c5c2" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Polygon Under the Action of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "baafa12f-49d2-5c88-8949-ad01d9c5840c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/866/Source/Images/q-12031-a-2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084622} {:answer/id #uuid "f4e832b2-3d84-5943-b50a-0ae01be865c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/866/Source/Images/q-12031-a-5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084623} {:answer/id #uuid "22a796a5-ec4c-5294-b684-ea68b71ee31d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/866/Source/Images/q-12031-a-3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084624} {:answer/id #uuid "2f3cc215-f2af-5f5d-a703-a92eb743ff27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/866/Source/Images/q-12031-a-1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084625} {:answer/id #uuid "565c9abe-f061-553c-ae9b-7dc7be9af98d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/866/Source/Images/q-12031-a-4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084626}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f3cc215-f2af-5f5d-a703-a92eb743ff27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/866/Source/Images/q-12031-a-1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084625} :answer-field/id #uuid "b619b9f8-236a-5fdb-b37b-dfe52a32b1fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084621}] :question/id #uuid "78cb91d8-8f98-5fe2-a9d0-7026936af122" :question/math-academy-id "q-12031" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/866/Source/Images/q-12031.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T$, given by\n$T = \\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown above. Which of the following is $△A^{′}B^{′}C^{′}$, the image of $△ABC$ under the action of $T$?"}]}
